  "$comment": "Canonical channel-open payer proof. The PAYING wallet signs `message` with EIP-191 personal_sign to claim a deposit; the hub recovers the signer and refuses to credit unless it matches the on-chain payer. Every SDK MUST reproduce `message` byte for byte.",
  "domain": "AIMarket-Payer-Proof",
  "version": 1,
  "purpose": "channel-open",
  "canonicalisation": {
    "chain": "trimmed, lowercased",
    "tx_hash": "if the body is hex: '0x' + lowercase(body) \u2014 the 0x prefix is normalised IN, not just the case. Non-hex (base58) is left byte-exact.",
    "payer": "a 42-char 0x hex address is lowercased (EIP-55 case is a checksum, not identity); other handles keep their case",
    "amount_cents": "int(round(amount_usd * 100)) with Python's ROUND-HALF-TO-EVEN. 0.125 -> 12, not 13. JS/Dart/Rust round half away from zero and MUST implement banker's rounding to match."
  },
  "signing": "EIP-191: keccak256('\\x19Ethereum Signed Message:\\n' + len(message) + message)",
